-- title:
--   Non-vanishing of the weight-zero minor-section archimedean zeta integral
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field with $[K:\mathbb{Q}]=3$ and let $\mu$ be an admissible twist of $K$, i.e. a continuous homomorphism $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times\to\mathbb{C}^\times$ trivial on $K^\times$ and of absolute value $1$. Suppose data $u_{\mathbb{R}}(w),a_{\mathbb{R}}(w)\in\mathbb{C}\times\mathbb{Z}/2$ at the real places and $u_{\mathbb{C}}(w),k_{\mathbb{C}}(w)\in\mathbb{C}\times\mathbb{Z}$ at the complex places describe the archimedean local components of $\mu$ through `IsArchCompAt`, and that $\omega$ is a character of $(\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q})^\times$ whose component at the real place has exponent $\sum_w u_{\mathbb{R}}(w)+\sum_w 2u_{\mathbb{C}}(w)$ and twist $\sum_w a_{\mathbb{R}}(w)+\sum_w (k_{\mathbb{C}}(w)+1)$. Let $E$ be a homomorphism from the infinite ideles of $\mathbb{Q}$ to the ideles splitting the infinite part and with trivial finite part, $a\in\mathbb{Q}^\times$ with an infinite idele $a_\infty$ above it, $\psi_\infty=\psi_{\mathrm{arch}}(a\,\cdot)$, $\nu_{\mathrm{add}}$ the scaled transported Lebesgue measure as prescribed, and $\nu_{\mathrm{mul}}$ a Haar measure on the infinite ideles units (the conclusion involves $\nu_{\mathrm{mul}}$ only). Let $w_0$ be a real place and let $P_2$ be the archimedean parameter of the remaining places, either principal from the two other real places, or, when only one complex place $w_C$ remains, discrete of weight $|k_{\mathbb{C}}(w_C)|$ if $k_{\mathbb{C}}(w_C)\neq 0$ and $\mathrm{principal}(u_{\mathbb{C}},0,u_{\mathbb{C}},1)$ otherwise. Let $D$ be an `ArchDatumR` for $P_2$ whose Whittaker function transforms under `rowIsometrySubgroup₀ ℝ` by `archWeightCharℝ k₀`, is a Casimir eigenfunction with eigenvalue $P_2$'s Laplace eigenvalue, and is not identically zero, with $k_0$ minimal in the stated sense ($k_0\in\{0,1\}$ and $k_0\equiv a_1+a_2$ in the principal case, $k_0=m+1$ in the discrete case), and assume $k_0=0$ and that $a_{\mathbb{R}}(w_0)\neq a_1$ whenever $P_2=\mathrm{principal}(u_1,a_1,u_2,a_2)$. Let $S$ be the minor Schwartz section $S(M)=\bigl((M_{00}-iM_{01})M_{12}-(M_{10}-iM_{11})M_{02}\bigr)\,\mathrm{gaussian3}(M)$ on $2\times 3$ real matrices. Then there exist an admissible twist $\sigma$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ and $s\in\mathbb{C}$ such that the $GL_3\times GL_1$ archimedean zeta integral `archZeta30` of the Jacquet vector $\mathrm{jacquetVector3}\,D\,(u_{\mathbb{R}}(w_0))\,(a_{\mathbb{R}}(w_0))\,a\,\psi_\infty\,S$ against $\sigma\circ E$, taken at $s$ and at the identity, is non-zero.
--
--   This is the archimedean non-vanishing input for the minor Schwartz section in the cubic-induction Rankin–Selberg construction: the weight-zero case, in which the remaining archimedean parameter is principal with a common sign differing from the sign at $w_0$. It is used in the unfolding step that matches the archimedean zeta integral of the induced $GL_3$ Whittaker vector with the expected gamma factor.
